      "text": "The village burial register, kept in a careful hand that grows less careful toward the end. The last entries are a widow, an infant and a woodcutter, each with the words 'buried in daylight'. On the newest line someone has written DORU, son of Donavich, then scored it out so hard the nib tore the page. Under it, smaller: not yet. Not yet. Not yet."
